From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Tue, 17 Sep 2024 04:54:04 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: fix single SKU power limits

In PSD countries the driver, not the firmware, compensates the OFDM
limits with the full-bandwidth EHT limits of the channel width, and
Canada joins the list of PSD countries. The path table is on only if
the device tree has a path entry for a channel. Each SKU table upload
takes the power that mac80211 configures, capped by the limit of the
current channel. The power of the last channel would otherwise lower
the cap of the next channel, for example after a scan, and a country
change would raise the cap above the configured power.

The mt7915 counterpart of this patch moves the 6 GHz LPI flags from
the device to the phy. This patch converts the mt7996 users of the
flags from the device to the phy, so that the patch "wifi: mt76:
mt7996: add LPI PSD limit and mgmt enhancement" builds, and the LPI
beacon rate override applies only to its band. It also fixes the other
build errors of that patch and a read of an uninitialized power offset
in the txpower vendor command, which now selects the radio with
RADIO_IDX instead of LINK_ID, to match hostapd. The command now holds
the device mutex: otherwise a scan or a channel set can change the
channel while it updates the power limits.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
